  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "A tank initially contains 100 L of water. After the tap is opened, the amount of water decreases at a constant rate. The table below shows: at \\(t=0,2,4\\) minutes, the water volume is \\(Q=100,90,80\\) liters, respectively. When the water volume is 40 liters, how many minutes is \\(t\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "12",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The water volume decreases by 5 liters per minute, so \\(Q=100-5t\\). Setting \\(Q=40\\) gives \\(t=12\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Scale equal drainage intervals\n\nAt a constant rate, the tank loses \\(100-90=10\\) L in every 2 minutes. Reaching 40 L means losing \\(100-40=60\\) L, which is \\(60\\div10=6\\) such amounts. Therefore the elapsed time is \\(6\\times2=12\\) minutes.",
